      <activity id="abde7214-9eff-5f80-9102-9706e09f03a4" activityNameId="6fd63eee-10da-5da4-86bf-4deab9fa7ff4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, building, window frame, wood, natural/varnished, wall opening, to final disposal</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, building, window frame, wood, natural/varnished, wall opening, to final disposal
The amount of materials to be disposed of at the end of life was estimated based on the bill of materials. A cut-off approach is used for recycling of metals (aluminium and zinc). The functional unit is 1m2 of wall opening.;
UUID: 12831aed-fe8c-42c1-a4aa-2f847fed7136
Included processes are the disposal of wood, glue, steel, plastics, paint, rubber. The transport to the municipal incineration plant is included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_12831aed-fe8c-42c1-a4aa-2f847fed7136.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
